~ crescent_start
Crescent Captain: …
Crescent Captain: So.
Crescent Captain: The armor reaches the Gate at last.

Crescent Captain: You move differently now.
Crescent Captain: Slower.
Crescent Captain: Heavier.

Crescent Captain: You’ve bled.
Crescent Captain: You’ve hesitated.
Crescent Captain: You’ve buried things you weren’t meant to lose.

Crescent Captain: I wondered how long it would take before you remembered.
Crescent Captain: Or before the memories broke you.

Crescent Captain: Or should I say—
Crescent Captain: Commander of the Broken Path.

Crescent Captain: You wore that title once.
Crescent Captain: You led monsters without mercy.
Crescent Captain: And you obeyed without question.

Crescent Captain: The Archivist is silent now.
Crescent Captain: Did you feel it when you struck it?
Crescent Captain: That pause?
Crescent Captain: That moment where your hands moved faster than your mind?

Crescent Captain: Good.
Crescent Captain: That means the armor still listens to you.

Crescent Captain: You met the healer.
Crescent Captain: The old one with the broken blade.
Crescent Captain: He tried to stitch something back together, didn’t he?

Crescent Captain: And the Deflector…
Crescent Captain: Always running.
Crescent Captain: Always refusing to choose.

Crescent Captain: And your mother.

Crescent Captain: …Ah.
Crescent Captain: Even now, I can see where it cracked you.

Crescent Captain: The monsters don’t attack you anymore.
Crescent Captain: The roads bend away from your steps.
Crescent Captain: You could end this war.

Crescent Captain: Or rule it.

Crescent Captain: Or abandon it —
Crescent Captain: like you almost did before.

Crescent Captain: Choose.

- 🔴 Destroy the Order => crescent_destroy
- 🔵 Take Control => crescent_control
- ⚫ Walk Away => crescent_walk_away


~ crescent_destroy
Player: This ends now.

Crescent Captain: …I was afraid you’d say that.

Crescent Captain: You’ve been listening to ghosts.
Crescent Captain: A mother who couldn’t stop you.
Crescent Captain: A monk who forgave too easily.
Crescent Captain: A creature you killed before it finished speaking.

Crescent Captain: Hope is a dangerous thing, Commander.
Crescent Captain: It teaches people to believe suffering was meaningless.

do GameState.full_attack.emit()
[wait=0.3]
do GameState.crescent_captain_attack.emit()
[wait=1]
- [Attack]
do GameState.full_attack.emit()
[wait=0.3]
do GameState.crescent_captain_attack.emit()  
[wait=1]
- [Attack]
do GameState.full_attack.emit()
[wait=0.3]
do GameState.crescent_captain_die.emit()  

Crescent Captain: [wait=2] The monsters will forget their masters.
The roads will belong to anyone strong enough to take them.

Crescent Captain: [wait=2] 
Freedom will be loud.
Messy.
Unforgiving.

Crescent Captain:
Let’s see if the world survives your mercy.
[wait=0.1]
do GameState.show_final_scene.emit()  

=> END

~ crescent_control
Player: Step aside.
Player: This Order will stand — but not under you.

Crescent Captain: …
Crescent Captain: Still choosing responsibility over innocence.

Crescent Captain: You always did.
Even before the armor.
Even before the blood.

Crescent Captain: The Archivist preserved knowledge.
The healer preserved bodies.
The Deflector preserved himself.

Crescent Captain: You preserve order.

Crescent Captain: Fear.
Structure.
Silence.

- [Attack]
do GameState.full_attack.emit()
[wait=1]
do GameState.crescent_captain_die.emit()

Crescent Captain: [wait=2] Just remember…
Crescent Captain: Orders don’t corrupt people.
Crescent Captain: They reveal them.

Crescent Captain: The Crescent bows.
do GameState.show_final_scene.emit()  
=> END


~ crescent_walk_away
Player: I’m done choosing sides.

Crescent Captain: …
Crescent Captain: Then why keep the armor?
Crescent Captain: It only listens to those who intend to rule.

Player: That’s why I’m leaving it.

Crescent Captain: You’d walk away from power?
Crescent Captain: From fear itself?

Player: Yes.

Crescent Captain: …
Crescent Captain: Then go.

Crescent Captain:
The Order will rot without you.
Or replace me.
Or become something worse.

Crescent Captain: The world will decide what follows.

do GameState.show_final_scene.emit()  

=> END
